.policy "fastapi-practice-response-exposes-secret-field" revision 1
.description "Declare a FastAPI route's response model without the password hash or the stored keys and secrets of a database row, so clients never receive them."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. FastAPI's response model is its output filter: what a route returns is validated
// into the model and serialized with the model's fields only. A route whose response model declares a password hash,
// an API key or a secret, or a route with no response model that returns the ORM row itself, sends that value to every
// client that can call it (FastAPI's Response Model docs: "could be sending our user's passwords to every client";
// OWASP API3, Broken Object Property Level Authorization).
//
// Reported, at the response model or at the `return`:
//   1. a route's response model (`response_model=X`, else its return annotation) names a class that declares a secret
//      field, also inside `List[X]`, `list[X]`, `Page[X]`, `Optional[X]`, `X | None` and module aliases of them;
//   2. a route with no response model (no `response_model=` and no return annotation, `-> Any`, or
//      `response_model=None`) returns a model instance whose class declares one: `db.get(User, id)` (awaited too),
//      `db.query(User)....first()/one()/all()/...`, `session.exec(select(User)).first()`, `session.scalars(...)` and
//      a result name assigned from `session.execute(select(User))`, `User(...)`, a parameter its dependency fills
//      (`current_user: CurrentUser`), a call of a function annotated to return an ORM model, or a local name whose
//      last assignment before the `return` is one of those.
// A class declares a field when its body or a base class's in the run assigns or annotates the name: SQLAlchemy
// `Column(...)`/`mapped_column(...)`/`Mapped[...]`, SQLModel and pydantic fields. Names are read as words (rse_hash_name,
// rse_key_name below), and a bool field is a flag, never a value:
//   - a password or its hash (`password`, `hashed_password`, `password_digest`, `user_pwd_hash`): in any model;
//   - a stored key, secret or token (`api_key`, `secret_key`, `access_token`, names ending in `_secret`, `_api_key`,
//     `_private_key`, `_password`): only on an ORM model (a table: `__tablename__`, `table=True`, a `Column`/
//     `mapped_column`/`Mapped` field, a SQLAlchemy declarative base), the stored row sent as it is. A pydantic schema
//     written to carry one is a design choice: a login route's Token, a new API key shown once, a TOTP enrolment
//     secret, Stripe's client_secret that the browser needs (polar's 31 such routes).
//   @router.get("/me", response_model=UserInDB)   # UserInDB declares hashed_password     reported
//   def me(current_user: CurrentUser): return current_user   # no response model           reported
//   @router.get("/me", response_model=UserPublic)  # without the field                     not reported
//   @router.post("/login", response_model=Token)    # access_token on a token schema        not reported
// Left alone: what pydantic never sends as is, resolved through imports (aliases included, another library's
// look-alike excluded): fields typed SecretStr/SecretBytes or ClassVar, a PlainSerializer/WrapSerializer in the
// field's metadata, `Field(exclude=True)`, a field a `@field_serializer` of the class (or a base) names, every field
// of a class with a `@model_serializer`; a route whose `response_model_exclude` names the field or whose
// `response_model_include` leaves it out (either one written as a variable counts as filtering); names that only
// contain a secret word (`password_changed_at`, `secret_name`); bool fields (`has_password: bool`,
// `is_secret = Column(Boolean)`); request bodies; hand-built `Response`/`JSONResponse` objects; `select(User.email)`
// and multi-entity rows; test files. A `password` field a schema declares on purpose (a device password the owner
// asked to see) is reported; the message says to leave it.
// Gaps: secret fields of nested models (`owner: User` inside the response model); dicts and lists built around a row
// (`{"user": user}`) and `jsonable_encoder(row)`; generic CRUD helpers whose return type is a TypeVar, and untyped
// helpers (`crud.get_account(db, id)` without `-> Account`); a field renamed by `Column("password")`; pydantic v1
// `Config.fields` exclusions.

#include "lib/fastapi.rerail"

// A model class, its bases and the aliases naming it may sit in other modules than the route (decision 0691: no node
// crosses files). Each class's file states its fields, serializers and table marks by the class's symbol
// (rse_field_at, ...), each module its aliases' names (rse_alias_names) and its defs' return annotations
// (rse_ret_name); the relations over symbols below join them (rse_exposed, rse_name_cls), and the outputs read the
// answer at the route's own nodes.
.violation ResponseModelExposesSecret(at: node, model: symbol, name: symbol) "The response model `{model}` declares `{name}`, which FastAPI sends to every caller. Use a response model without it; leave it only if this route exists to show that value to its owner."
ResponseModelExposesSecret(r, m, x) :- rse_rm_name(f, dc, r, q0), rse_name_cls(q0, q), rse_exposed(q, x),
    !rse_excl_all(dc), !rse_excl_name(dc, x), !rse_incl(dc), fa_route(f, dc, k, _), fa_router_key(k, _), docof(f, d),
    !fa_test_doc(d), split_dot(q, _, m).
ResponseModelExposesSecret(r, m, x) :- rse_rm_name(f, dc, r, q0), rse_name_cls(q0, q), rse_exposed(q, x),
    !rse_excl_all(dc), !rse_excl_name(dc, x), rse_incl_name(dc, x), fa_route(f, dc, k, _), fa_router_key(k, _),
    docof(f, d), !fa_test_doc(d), split_dot(q, _, m).

.violation RouteReturnsSecret(at: node, model: symbol, name: symbol) "This route has no response model and returns a `{model}`, so its `{name}` reaches every caller. Declare a response model without it; leave it only if the route exists to show it to its owner."
RouteReturnsSecret(r, m, x) :- rse_ret(f, r, e), rse_inst(e, "cls", q), rse_exposed(q, x), rse_raw_route(f, k),
    fa_router_key(k, _), docof(f, d), !fa_test_doc(d), split_dot(q, _, m).
// A parameter whose annotation names an `Annotated[T, Depends(...)]` alias of another module (`current_user:
// CurrentUser`): T's class (lib/fastapi's fa_var_type), when the alias holds a Depends call (rse_dep_alias).
RouteReturnsSecret(r, m, x) :- rse_ret(f, r, e), rse_inst(e, "palias", aq), rse_dep_alias(aq), fa_var_type(aq, q),
    rse_exposed(q, x), rse_raw_route(f, k), fa_router_key(k, _), docof(f, d), !fa_test_doc(d), split_dot(q, _, m).
// A call of a function of the run annotated to return an ORM model (`-> Optional[User]`, `-> list[User]`).
RouteReturnsSecret(r, m, x) :- rse_ret(f, r, e), rse_inst(e, "ret", g), rse_ret_name(g, q0), rse_name_cls(q0, q),
    rse_orm(q), rse_exposed(q, x), rse_raw_route(f, k), fa_router_key(k, _), docof(f, d), !fa_test_doc(d),
    split_dot(q, _, m).

// ---- secret fields -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Field names are read as words. Python has no type for "a secret", so the rule matches the words a password, its
// hash, a key or a secret is named with (a name list, kept because nothing better is decidable), and settles the rest
// by type: a field typed `bool` (or a `Boolean` column, or a True/False default) is a flag, never a value.
// rse_hash_glob(g): a password or its hash, in any model: `password`, `passwd`, or a password word (password, passwd,
// pwd, pw) and a hash word (hash, hashed, digest) joined in either order, with any prefix (`user_password_hash`).
.decl rse_pw_word(w: symbol)
rse_pw_word("password"). rse_pw_word("passwd"). rse_pw_word("pwd"). rse_pw_word("pw").
.decl rse_hash_word(w: symbol)
rse_hash_word("hash"). rse_hash_word("hashed"). rse_hash_word("digest").
.decl rse_hash_glob(g: symbol)
rse_hash_glob("password"). rse_hash_glob("passwd").
rse_hash_glob(g) :- rse_pw_word(p), rse_hash_word(h), (g = cat(p, cat("_", h)) ; g = cat("*_", cat(p, cat("_", h))) ;
    g = cat(h, cat("_", p)) ; g = cat("*_", cat(h, cat("_", p)))).
// rse_key_glob(g): a key, secret, token or plain password the server stores: `secret`, `api_key`, `apikey`,
// `secret_key`, `private_key`, `access_token`, `refresh_token`, and names ending in `_secret`, `_api_key`,
// `_secret_key`, `_private_key`, `_password` or `_passwd` (`webhook_secret`, `openai_api_key`, `smtp_password`). A
// response schema written to show one (a new API key shown once, a TOTP enrolment secret, Stripe's client_secret meant
// for the browser) is a design choice, so these count only on an ORM model: the stored row sent as it is.
.decl rse_key_glob(g: symbol)
rse_key_glob("secret"). rse_key_glob("api_key"). rse_key_glob("apikey"). rse_key_glob("secret_key").
rse_key_glob("private_key"). rse_key_glob("access_token"). rse_key_glob("refresh_token").
rse_key_glob("*_secret"). rse_key_glob("*_api_key"). rse_key_glob("*_secret_key"). rse_key_glob("*_private_key").
rse_key_glob("*_password"). rse_key_glob("*_passwd").
// rse_class_stmt(c, a): assignment or bare annotation a sits directly in class c's body.
.decl rse_class_stmt(c: node, a: node)
rse_class_stmt(c, a) :- kind(a, "assignment"), scope_node(a, c), kind(c, "class_definition").
// rse_cand(c, x, a): class c's body binds name x at a.
.decl rse_cand(c: node, x: symbol, a: node)
rse_cand(c, x, a) :- rse_class_stmt(c, a), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x).
// rse_secret_at(a, k): the name bound at a is a password or its hash (k "hash") or a stored key (k "key").
.decl rse_hash_at(a: node)
rse_hash_at(a) :- rse_cand(_, x, a), rse_hash_glob(g), glob(g, x).
.decl rse_secret_at(a: node, k: symbol)
rse_secret_at(a, "hash") :- rse_hash_at(a).
rse_secret_at(a, "key") :- rse_cand(_, x, a), rse_key_glob(g), glob(g, x), !rse_hash_at(a).
// rse_field(c, x, a, k): class c's body declares secret field x at a (`x = v`, `x: T = v`, `x: T`), not a flag.
.decl rse_field(c: node, x: symbol, a: node, k: symbol)
rse_field(c, x, a, k) :- rse_cand(c, x, a), rse_secret_at(a, k), !rse_flag(a).
// rse_flag(a): the field holds a bool: typed `bool` (`Mapped[bool]`), a `Boolean` column, or a True/False default.
.decl rse_flag(a: node)
rse_flag(a) :- rse_cand(_, _, a), field(a, "type", t), (n = t ; within(n, t)), leaf_name(n, "bool").
rse_flag(a) :- rse_cand(_, _, a), field(a, "right", v), (n = v ; within(n, v)), leaf_name(n, "Boolean").
rse_flag(a) :- rse_cand(_, _, a), field(a, "right", v), (kind(v, "true") ; kind(v, "false")).
// rse_hidden(a): pydantic never serializes the field as is, resolved through imports: typed SecretStr/SecretBytes
// (masked) or ClassVar (no field), a PlainSerializer/WrapSerializer in its Annotated metadata, or
// `Field(exclude=True)` as its value or in its metadata. A name that resolves to nothing (a star import) is read by its
// last part.
.decl rse_hidden_q(q: symbol)
rse_hidden_q("pydantic.SecretStr"). rse_hidden_q("pydantic.types.SecretStr"). rse_hidden_q("pydantic.SecretBytes").
rse_hidden_q("pydantic.types.SecretBytes"). rse_hidden_q("typing.ClassVar"). rse_hidden_q("typing_extensions.ClassVar").
rse_hidden_q("pydantic.v1.SecretStr"). rse_hidden_q("pydantic.v1.SecretBytes").
rse_hidden_q("pydantic.PlainSerializer"). rse_hidden_q("pydantic.functional_serializers.PlainSerializer").
rse_hidden_q("pydantic.WrapSerializer"). rse_hidden_q("pydantic.functional_serializers.WrapSerializer").
.decl rse_hidden_leaf(x: symbol)
rse_hidden_leaf("SecretStr"). rse_hidden_leaf("SecretBytes"). rse_hidden_leaf("ClassVar").
.decl rse_hidden(a: node)
rse_hidden(a) :- rse_field(_, _, a, _), field(a, "type", t), (n = t ; within(n, t)), sym_of(n, q), rse_hidden_q(q).
rse_hidden(a) :- rse_field(_, _, a, _), field(a, "type", t), (n = t ; within(n, t)), !sym_of(n, _), leaf_name(n, x),
    rse_hidden_leaf(x).
rse_hidden(a) :- rse_field(_, _, a, _), kind(k, "call"), within(k, a), rse_field_call(k), call_arg(k, -1, "exclude", v),
    kind(v, "true").
.decl rse_field_call(k: node)
rse_field_call(k) :- kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "pydantic.Field" ; q = "pydantic.fields.Field" ; q = "sqlmodel.Field" ; q = "sqlmodel.main.Field").
rse_field_call(k) :- kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", f), !sym_of(f, _), call_name(k, "Field").
// rse_serializer(c, k): a method of class c is decorated with pydantic's field_serializer call k (through imports,
// aliases included; another library's `field_serializer` is not one).
.decl rse_serializer(c: node, k: node)
rse_serializer(c, k) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), decorator(f, e), unparen(e, k), kind(k, "call"),
    field(k, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), rse_ser_q(q, "field"), nearest(f, c, scope), kind(c, "class_definition").
// rse_model_serializer(c): a method of class c is decorated with pydantic's model_serializer, bare or called.
.decl rse_model_serializer(c: node)
rse_model_serializer(c) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), decorator(f, e), unparen(e, k), sym_of(k, q),
    rse_ser_q(q, "model"), nearest(f, c, scope), kind(c, "class_definition").
rse_model_serializer(c) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), decorator(f, e), unparen(e, k), kind(k, "call"),
    field(k, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q), rse_ser_q(q, "model"), nearest(f, c, scope), kind(c, "class_definition").
.decl rse_ser_q(q: symbol, k: symbol)
rse_ser_q("pydantic.field_serializer", "field"). rse_ser_q("pydantic.functional_serializers.field_serializer", "field").
rse_ser_q("pydantic.model_serializer", "model"). rse_ser_q("pydantic.functional_serializers.model_serializer", "model").

// ---- classes, by symbol ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stated in each class's file: rse_field_at(b, x, h, k): class b declares secret field x of kind k, hidden (h "1") or
// not ("0"); rse_ser_at(b, x): a `@field_serializer("x", ...)` of b decides how x is sent (`mask` returning "***");
// rse_mser_at(b): a `@model_serializer` of b decides every field; rse_orm_own_at(b): b's own definition makes it a
// table; rse_cls(b): b is a class of the run.
.decl rse_field_at(b: symbol, x: symbol, h: symbol, k: symbol)
rse_field_at(b, x, "1", k) :- rse_field(c, x, a, k), rse_hidden(a), class_def(c, b).
rse_field_at(b, x, "0", k) :- rse_field(c, x, a, k), !rse_hidden(a), class_def(c, b).
.decl rse_ser_at(b: symbol, x: symbol)
rse_ser_at(b, x) :- rse_serializer(c, k), call_arg(k, _, "", s), str(s, x), class_def(c, b).
.decl rse_mser_at(b: symbol)
rse_mser_at(b) :- rse_model_serializer(c), class_def(c, b).
.decl rse_cls(b: symbol)
rse_cls(b) :- class_def(c, b).
// rse_anc(q, b): b is q or one of its bases, in the run or not (python/scopes' subclass, over symbols).
.decl rse_anc(q: symbol, b: symbol)
rse_anc(q, q) :- rse_cls(q).
rse_anc(q, b) :- subclass(q, b).
// rse_exposed(q, x): class q, or a base of it in the run, declares secret field x, and none of them hides it; a key
// name counts only when q is an ORM model.
.decl rse_declares(q: symbol, x: symbol, k: symbol)
rse_declares(q, x, k) :- rse_anc(q, b), rse_field_at(b, x, "0", k).
.decl rse_hides(q: symbol, x: symbol)
rse_hides(q, x) :- rse_anc(q, b), rse_field_at(b, x, "1", _).
rse_hides(q, x) :- rse_declares(q, x, _), rse_anc(q, b), rse_ser_at(b, x).
rse_hides(q, x) :- rse_declares(q, x, _), rse_anc(q, b), rse_mser_at(b).
.decl rse_exposed(q: symbol, x: symbol)
rse_exposed(q, x) :- rse_declares(q, x, "hash"), !rse_hides(q, x).
rse_exposed(q, x) :- rse_declares(q, x, "key"), !rse_hides(q, x), rse_orm(q).

// ---- ORM models --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rse_orm_own(c): class c's own definition makes it a table: `table=True` (SQLModel), `__tablename__`, a
// `Column(...)`/`mapped_column(...)` value or a `Mapped[...]` annotation.
.decl rse_orm_own(c: node)
rse_orm_own(c) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, k, _),
    kind(k, "keyword_argument"), field(k, "name", n), text(n, "table"), field(k, "value", v), kind(v, "true").
rse_orm_own(c) :- rse_class_stmt(c, a), field(a, "left", l), text(l, "__tablename__").
rse_orm_own(c) :- rse_class_stmt(c, a), field(a, "right", v), kind(v, "call"),
    (call_name(v, "Column") ; call_name(v, "mapped_column")).
rse_orm_own(c) :- rse_class_stmt(c, a), field(a, "type", t), (n = t ; within(n, t)), leaf_name(n, "Mapped").
.decl rse_orm_own_at(b: symbol)
rse_orm_own_at(b) :- rse_orm_own(c), class_def(c, b).
.decl rse_orm_base(q: symbol)
rse_orm_base("sqlalchemy.orm.DeclarativeBase"). rse_orm_base("sqlalchemy.orm.DeclarativeBaseNoMeta").
rse_orm_base("sqlalchemy.orm.decl_api.DeclarativeBase").
// rse_decl_base(b): module variable b is `declarative_base()`, stated in its file.
.decl rse_decl_base(b: symbol)
rse_decl_base(b) :- fa_module_var(b, v), kind(v, "call"), call_name(v, "declarative_base").
.decl rse_orm(q: symbol)
rse_orm(q) :- rse_anc(q, b), rse_orm_own_at(b).
rse_orm(q) :- subclass(q, b), rse_orm_base(b).
// `Base = declarative_base()` in any module of the run.
rse_orm(q) :- subclass(q, b), rse_decl_base(b).

// ---- response models ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rse_rm(f, dc, r): route f's response model is type expression r: `response_model=` of its decorator dc, else its
// return annotation.
.decl rse_rm(f: node, dc: node, r: node)
rse_rm(f, dc, r) :- fa_route(f, dc, _, _), fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model", r), !kind(r, "none").
rse_rm(f, dc, r) :- fa_route(f, dc, _, _), !fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model", _), field(f, "return_type", t0),
    fa_strip(t0, r).
// rse_troot(r): a type expression whose classes the rule reads: response models, every def's return annotation (the
// def a raw route calls may be in any module), and the value of a module alias (`UserList = list[UserInDB]`).
.decl rse_troot(r: node)
rse_troot(r) :- rse_rm(_, _, r).
rse_troot(r) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), field(g, "return_type", t0), fa_strip(t0, r).
rse_troot(v) :- rse_alias_val(_, v).
.decl rse_alias_val(aq: symbol, v: node)
rse_alias_val(aq, v) :- fa_module_var(aq, v0), fa_strip(v0, v),
    (kind(v, "subscript") ; kind(v, "generic_type") ; kind(v, "binary_operator")).
// rse_tx(r, e): e is r, or a type argument inside it: `List[X]`, `Page[X]`, `Optional[X]`, `X | None`, the type of
// `Annotated[X, ...]`, the value of a module alias of this file. An alias of another module is followed by symbol
// (rse_name_cls).
.decl rse_tx(r: node, e: node)
rse_tx(r, r) :- rse_troot(r).
rse_tx(r, a) :- rse_tx(r, m), rse_targ(m, a).
rse_tx(r, v) :- rse_tx(r, m), (kind(m, "identifier") ; kind(m, "attribute")), fa_value(m, v0), fa_strip(v0, v),
    (kind(v, "subscript") ; kind(v, "generic_type") ; kind(v, "binary_operator")).
.decl rse_targ(m: node, a: node)
rse_targ(m, a) :- kind(m, "subscript"), !fa_annotated(m, _, _), field(m, "subscript", e), fa_strip(e, a).
rse_targ(m, a) :- kind(m, "generic_type"), !fa_annotated(m, _, _), child(m, p, 1), kind(p, "type_parameter"),
    child(p, t, _), fa_strip(t, a).
rse_targ(m, a) :- fa_annotated(m, a, _).
rse_targ(m, a) :- (kind(m, "binary_operator") ; kind(m, "union_type")), child(m, e, _), fa_strip(e, a).
// rse_tname(r, q): type expression r names q, itself or in a type argument (rse_tx).
.decl rse_tname(r: node, q: symbol)
rse_tname(r, q) :- rse_tx(r, e), (kind(e, "identifier") ; kind(e, "attribute")), sym_of(e, q).
// rse_rm_name(f, dc, r, q): route f's response model r names q. rse_ret_name(g, q): def g's return annotation names
// q. rse_alias_names(aq, q): module alias aq's value names q. Each stated in its file; rse_name_cls(q0, q) follows
// the names through the aliases, by symbol: q0 itself, or what an alias it names names.
.decl rse_rm_name(f: node, dc: node, r: node, q: symbol)
rse_rm_name(f, dc, r, q) :- rse_rm(f, dc, r), rse_tname(r, q).
.decl rse_ret_name(g: symbol, q: symbol)
rse_ret_name(gq, q) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), field(g, "return_type", t0), fa_strip(t0, r), rse_tname(r, q),
    pt_def(g, gq).
.decl rse_alias_names(aq: symbol, q: symbol)
rse_alias_names(aq, q) :- rse_alias_val(aq, v), rse_tname(v, q).
.decl rse_name_need(q: symbol)
rse_name_need(q) :- rse_rm_name(_, _, _, q).
rse_name_need(q) :- rse_ret_name(_, q).
.decl rse_name_cls(q0: symbol, q: symbol)
rse_name_cls(q0, q0) :- rse_name_need(q0).
rse_name_cls(q0, q) :- rse_name_cls(q0, q1), rse_alias_names(q1, q).
// rse_excl_name(dc, x), rse_excl_all(dc), rse_incl(dc), rse_incl_name(dc, x): route call dc filters field x out
// itself when `response_model_exclude` names it, or is no literal (a variable filters every field), or
// `response_model_include` is given (a variable too) and does not name it.
.decl rse_mentions(v: node, x: symbol)
rse_mentions(v, x) :- fa_route_kw(_, _, v), (s = v ; within(s, v)), str(s, x), (rse_hash_glob(g) ; rse_key_glob(g)),
    glob(g, x).
.decl rse_literal(v: node)
rse_literal(v) :- kind(v, "set") ; kind(v, "dictionary") ; kind(v, "list") ; kind(v, "tuple").
.decl rse_excl_name(dc: node, x: symbol)
rse_excl_name(dc, x) :- fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model_exclude", v), rse_mentions(v, x).
.decl rse_excl_all(dc: node)
rse_excl_all(dc) :- fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model_exclude", v), !rse_literal(v).
.decl rse_incl(dc: node)
rse_incl(dc) :- fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model_include", _).
.decl rse_incl_name(dc: node, x: symbol)
rse_incl_name(dc, x) :- fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model_include", v), rse_mentions(v, x).

// ---- raw returns -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rse_raw_route(f, k): route f, on key k, has no response model: no `response_model=` and no return annotation (or
// `-> Any`), or `response_model=None`.
.decl rse_raw_route(f: node, k: symbol)
rse_raw_route(f, k) :- fa_route(f, dc, k, _), !fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model", _), !field(f, "return_type", _).
rse_raw_route(f, k) :- fa_route(f, dc, k, _), !fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model", _), field(f, "return_type", t0),
    fa_strip(t0, t), (text(t, "Any") ; text(t, "typing.Any")).
rse_raw_route(f, k) :- fa_route(f, dc, k, _), fa_route_kw(dc, "response_model", v), kind(v, "none").
// rse_val(e, v): e with parentheses and `await` off.
.decl rse_val(e: node, v: node)
rse_val(e, v) :- unparen(e, v), !kind(v, "await").
rse_val(e, v) :- unparen(e, a), kind(a, "await"), child(a, b, 0), rse_val(b, v).
// rse_ret(f, r, e): return statement r of raw route f returns expression e.
.decl rse_ret(f: node, r: node, e: node)
rse_ret(f, r, e) :- rse_raw_route(f, _), kind(r, "return_statement"), def_frame(r, f), child(r, e0, _),
    !kind(e0, "comment"), rse_val(e0, e).
// rse_need(e): an expression whose instance class the rule asks for: what a raw route returns, and the value a
// returned name was last assigned.
.decl rse_need(e: node)
rse_need(e) :- rse_ret(_, _, e).
rse_need(w) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), latest_assign(e, x, a), rasg(_, x, v, a),
    rse_val(v, w).
.decl rse_row_method(m: symbol)
rse_row_method("first"). rse_row_method("one"). rse_row_method("one_or_none"). rse_row_method("scalar_one").
rse_row_method("scalar_one_or_none"). rse_row_method("scalar"). rse_row_method("all"). rse_row_method("get").
// rse_entity_call(s, q): call s selects whole rows of q (a class, by rse_exposed): `select(User)`, `query(User)`, one
// entity only.
.decl rse_entity_call(s: node, q: symbol)
rse_entity_call(s, q) :- kind(s, "call"), (call_name(s, "select") ; call_name(s, "query")), call_arg(s, 0, "", a),
    !call_arg(s, 1, "", _), unparen(a, ae), sym_of(ae, q).
// rse_entity_in(o, q): the receiver chain o selects rows of q: the call is in o, or o's root name was last assigned
// a value that makes it (`result = await session.execute(select(User))`).
.decl rse_entity_in(o: node, q: symbol)
rse_entity_in(o, q) :- rse_row_call(_, o), (s = o ; within(s, o)), rse_entity_call(s, q).
rse_entity_in(o, q) :- rse_row_call(_, o), (n = o ; within(n, o)), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x),
    latest_assign(n, x, a), within(s, a), rse_entity_call(s, q).
// rse_row_call(e, o): needed call e is `o.<row method>(...)`.
.decl rse_row_call(e: node, o: node)
rse_row_call(e, o) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, m), rse_row_method(m).
// rse_inst(e, how, q): needed expression e holds an instance (or a list of instances): of class q (how "cls"; that q
// is a class is rse_exposed's), of the type an alias q of another module declares (how "palias"), or of what def q
// is annotated to return (how "ret").
.decl rse_inst(e: node, how: symbol, q: symbol)
rse_inst(e, "cls", q) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q).
rse_inst(e, "cls", q) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, _, "get"),
    call_arg(e, 0, "", a), unparen(a, ae), sym_of(ae, q).
rse_inst(e, "cls", q) :- rse_row_call(e, o), rse_entity_in(o, q).
rse_inst(e, how, q) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), latest_assign(e, x, a), rasg(_, x, v, a),
    rse_val(v, w), rse_inst(w, how, q).
// A parameter its dependency fills, never reassigned before the return: its type, or the alias of another module
// that declares both.
rse_inst(e, "cls", q) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), !latest_assign(e, x, _), look(e, x, f),
    fa_param_dep(f, _, x, _), fa_param_type(f, _, x, t), sym_of(t, q).
rse_inst(e, "palias", aq) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), !latest_assign(e, x, _), look(e, x, f),
    fa_param_alias(f, _, x, aq).
rse_inst(e, "ret", fq) :- rse_need(e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, fq).
// rse_dep_alias(aq): module alias aq holds a Depends call in its metadata, stated in its file.
.decl rse_dep_alias(aq: symbol)
rse_dep_alias(aq) :- fa_alias_dep(aq, _).

